        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.088,
            0.685,
            0.109
          ],
          "content": "8. In the following pattern, fill in the missing numbers:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.113,
            0.359,
            0.132
          ],
          "content": "**Ans.** $1 ^ { 2 } + 2 ^ { 2 } + 2 ^ { 2 } = 3 ^ { 2 }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.213,
            0.133,
            0.358,
            0.151
          ],
          "content": "2 ^ { 2 } + 3 ^ { 2 } + 6 ^ { 2 } = 7 ^ { 2 }",
          "image_source": "images/page_20_equation_2.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.213,
            0.153,
            0.382,
            0.171
          ],
          "content": "3^{2} + 4^{2} + 12^{2} = 13^{2}",
          "image_source": "images/page_20_equation_3.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.213,
            0.173,
            0.396,
            0.191
          ],
          "content": "4 ^ { 2 } + 5 ^ { 2 } + 2 0 ^ { 2 } = \\underline { { ( 2 1 ) ^ { 2 } } }",
          "image_source": "images/page_20_equation_4.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.213,
            0.193,
            0.419,
            0.212
          ],
          "content": "9 ^ { 2 } + 1 0 ^ { 2 } + \\underline { { ( 9 0 ) ^ { 2 } } } = \\underline { { ( 9 1 ) ^ { 2 } } }",
          "image_source": "images/page_20_equation_5.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.235,
            0.276,
            0.255
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Page No. 13"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.262,
            0.673,
            0.31
          ],
          "content": "Can a cube end with exactly two zeroes (00)? Explain. **Ans.** No"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.344,
            0.276,
            0.363
          ],
          "content": "**Page No. 14**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.371,
            0.734,
            0.418
          ],
          "content": "？ Can you tell what this sum is without doing the calculation? **Ans.** $1 0 ^ { 3 } = 1 0 0 0$"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.45,
            0.276,
            0.471
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Page No. 15"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.479,
            0.757,
            0.552
          ],
          "content": "Find the cube roots of these numbers: (i) $^ { 3 } \\sqrt { 6 4 } =$ (ii) $^ 3 \\sqrt { 5 1 2 } =$ (iii) $^ 3 \\sqrt { 7 2 9 } =$ **Ans.** (i) 4 (ii) 8 (iii) 9"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.572,
            0.276,
            0.593
          ],
          "content": "**Page No. 16**"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.611,
            0.293,
            0.634
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Figure it Out"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.643,
            0.781,
            0.689
          ],
          "content": "1. Find the cube roots of 27000 and 10648. **Ans.** (i) Cube root of 27000 = 30 (ii) Cube root of 10648 = 22"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.698,
            0.826,
            0.744
          ],
          "content": "2. What number will you multiply by 1323 to make it a cube number? **Ans.** 7"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.753,
            0.593,
            0.774
          ],
          "content": "3. State true or false. Explain your reasoning."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.203,
            0.777,
            0.611,
            0.798
          ],
          "content": "(i) The cube of any odd number is even."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.198,
            0.801,
            0.652,
            0.822
          ],
          "content": "(ii) There is no perfect cube that ends with 8."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.192,
            0.826,
            0.779,
            0.846
          ],
          "content": "(iii) The cube of a 2-digit number may be a 3-digit number."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.193,
            0.85,
            0.837,
            0.87
          ],
          "content": "(iv) The cube of a 2-digit number may have seven or more digits."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.198,
            0.874,
            0.701,
            0.894
          ],
          "content": "(v) Cube numbers have an odd number of factors"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.859,
            0.919,
            0.879,
            0.94
          ],
          "content": "3"
        }
